// Two sparks; the seeds wait in the far corners.
name Two Lanterns
rule B1/S
steps 3
hint Two sparks lit this. Two seeds lie in the corners, one each side. Each wall has a single gap.
tip Each set of rings is centred two cells diagonally from its spark, and the two sparks share a row.
intro Two seeds this time, and they are not together. Whoever carried them came from both ends of the world.
outro You carried what they carried, and stood where they stood.
